_writes\":\"A:minority-write,B:majority-write,C:minority-write,D:majority-write,E:majority-write\",\"healed_leaders\":\"C\",\"leader_config_ids_after_heal\":\"A,B,C,D,E\",\"leader_log_last_index\":13,\"local_id\":\"A\",\"log_last_indexes\":\"A:13,B:13,C:13,D:13,E:13\",\"lone_leader\":\"C\",\"mode\":\"defect_restart\",\"nodes_with_log_behind_leader\":0,\"post_heal_apply_error\":\"none\",\"same_term_conflicting_payload\":true}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('update.json'))\nd['rationale']=d['rationale']+\\\" The filed successor extends the live-cluster harness with FSM applied-state sampling at the healed phase: local feedback is deterministic across runs (A and C applied minority-write while B, D and E applied majority-write, with every node at log index 13 after healing), so the damage is in the applied state and not only in the stored entry bytes. Its three comparisons cover that observation; the ten earlier comparisons and their receipt remain with the previous experiment rather than being re-declared.\\\"\nd['experiment']={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"3eae8e12b0574799b781f10f7899dbad-question-0\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_stale_election_test.go\\\",\n \\\"execution_package\\\":\\\".\\\",\n \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"bff59e419ade4e618713d3fce3ff381e-experiment\\\",\n \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"Adds FSM applied-state sampling at the healed phase and three comparisons over it; the cluster scenario, the admission and the ten earlier comparisons are unchanged and remain recorded with the previous experiment and its receipt.\\\",\n \\\"semantic_changes\\\":[\\\"The healed event now also reports each node's applied command list (MockFSM applied data filtered to the two conflicting write payloads), whether those lists agree, and the restarted and majority nodes' applied writes.\\\",\n  \\\"Three comparisons are added over the healed event: the applied writes must agree across nodes, and the two operand comparisons confirming which write each side applied.\\\"],\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-scan\\\",\\\"s-restorecommitted\\\",\\\"s-processlogs\\\",\\\"s-confentry\\\",\\\"s-quorumsize\\\",\\\"s-votegrant\\\",\\\"s-staging\\\",\\\"s-dupskip\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Real 5-node in-memory cluster whose node A restarts with Config.RestoreCommittedLogs after a committed configuration change newer than its snapshot, splits {A,C} from {B,D,E} long enough for both sides to elect and commit a different entry at the same index and term, and is then healed; this revision samples each node's applied FSM commands after healing in addition to the log payloads.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"Cluster state is produced through normal operations only: BootstrapCluster({A,B,C}) from A, election, committed applies, a user snapshot on A, AddVoter(D), AddVoter(E) and a further apply.\\\",\n   \\\"A is shut down gracefully and restarted from its own store objects; all five nodes run with Config.RestoreCommittedLogs enabled so the persisted commit index the restart reads is the one the running protocol staged.\\\",\n   \\\"The partition and the healing are expressed only by transport disconnection and reconnection; timings, RPC lifecycles and election rules are untouched.\\\",\n   \\\"Applied state is read from the MockFSM that each node runs with, filtered to the two write payloads, after the partition is healed, one further entry is committed and 300 ms have passed.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No crash, storage fault, snapshot install or log compaction is exercised.\\\",\n   \\\"The no-feature restart control inside the cluster remains unexecuted.\\\",\n   \\\"No repository test was executed.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"cluster_ids\\\":\\\"A,B,C,D,E\\\",\\\"initial_configuration\\\":\\\"A,B,C\\\",\\\"added_voters\\\":\\\"D,E\\\",\\\"partition\\\":\\\"A,C | B,D,E\\\",\\\"conflict_index\\\":11,\\\"conflict_term\\\":3,\\\"minority_write\\\":\\\"minority-write\\\",\\\"majority_write\\\":\\\"majority-write\\\"}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"The harness builds five InmemTransports (A..E) in a full mesh with per-node InmemStore, InmemCommitTrackingStore and InmemSnapshotStore, bootstraps {A,B,C} from A, starts A, B and C with MockFSM and Config.RestoreCommittedLogs=true, waits for a leader, transfers leadership to A if needed, applies three commands, waits on a Barrier and takes a user snapshot on A. It starts D and E, adds each as voter through the leader, applies one further command and emits 'fixture'. It shuts A down, cuts {A,C} from {B,D,E}, reconnects A to C only, restarts A from the same stores and emits 'restart'. It waits for a leader in each partition, submits one Apply to each leader, reads both leaders' entries at the shared index and emits 'outcome'. It then reconnects the full mesh, waits for exactly one leader, applies one further entry, waits 300ms and emits 'healed' with the payloads and terms at the conflict index, payload consistency, same_term_conflicting_payload, log last indexes, the restarted node's and B's configurations, the leader's configuration, the number of nodes behind the leader, each node's applied write list, whether those lists agree, and post_heal_apply_error. All nodes are shut down afterwards. Event order: fixture, restart, outcome, healed.\\\",\n \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"hashicorp/raft AppendEntries log-matching and the FSM apply path: same-term duplicates are skipped, so the FSM state on the two sides keeps the entries their own leader committed.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"fixture\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[\n   {\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"defect_restart\\\"},\n   {\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshot_config_ids\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"A,B,C\\\"},\n   {\\\"field\\\":\\\"config_entry_ids\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"A,B,C,D,E\\\"},\n   {\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_reported_config_ids\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"A,B,C,D,E\\\"},\n   {\\\"field\\\":\\\"commit_covers_config_entry\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   {\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshot_before_config_entry\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}]}],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"healed\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"local_id\\\",\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"defect_restart\\\"}],\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"fsm_applied_consistent\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"After the partition is healed, every node's FSM should have applied the same commands at the index both leaders used.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"healed\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"local_id\\\",\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"defect_restart\\\"}],\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_fsm_applied_writes\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"minority-write\\\"},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Operand: the restarted node's FSM applied the minority write, which the current configuration's quorum never accepted.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"healed\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"local_id\\\",\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"adm_defect\\\",\\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"defect_restart\\\"}],\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"b_fsm_applied_writes\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"majority-write\\\"},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Operand: a node on the majority side applied the majority write at the same index.\\\"}]\n}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run && cp draft/work/zz_stale_test.go draft/assurance_stale_election_test.go && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -4\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
